/E (Entanglement is the ability of qubits to correlate their state with other qubits more strongly than regular probability allows. Entangled systems are so intrinsically linked that when quantum processors measure a single entangled qubit, they can immediately determine information about other qubits in the entangled system.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
