/E (An environment of entangled qubits placed into a state of collective superposition structures information in a way that looks like waves, with amplitudes associated with each outcome. These amplitudes become the probabilities of the outcomes of a measurement of the system. These waves can build on each other when many of them peak at a particular outcome \(Constructive Interference\), or cancel each other out when the peaks and troughs interact \(Destructive Interference\).)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
