/T (Classical vs. Quantum Computing)
/E (Classical vs. Quantum Computing)
/Alt ()
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
791 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A quantum computer, on the other hand, is like someone with magical abilities, who can somehow try all 1000 keys at once. Instead of checking each key individually, it explores multiple possibilities simultaneously. Thus it can find the correct key much faster. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
