/E (Again, Quantum Mechanics comes to our rescue. To date, traditional data encryption has generally been effective in maintaining secure communications in most cybersecurity settings. However, the rise of quantum computing has made even the most secure traditional cryptographic algorithms vulnerable. As discussed in the previous section, quantum computers can potentially solve complex problems orders of magnitude faster than our current fastest classical computers. While such computers were once only theoretical, experts now believe that it might be only 20 to 50 years away before we fully enter the quantum age.)
