/T (The conversation then shifted to the state of quantum computing education in India. Apoorva acknowledged a gap in the number of educators who can teach the subject of quantum computation from foundational principles. He stressed the importance of building a strong foundation, stating, "They might look at some top level research paper, and then teach content related to it. That is not equivalent to teaching the stuff from the basics.")
/E (The conversation then shifted to the state of quantum computing education in India. Apoorva acknowledged a gap in the number of educators who can teach the subject of quantum computation from foundational principles. He stressed the importance of building a strong foundation, stating, "They might look at some top level research paper, and then teach content related to it. That is not equivalent to teaching the stuff from the basics.")
/Alt ()
/Pg 57 0 R
